Fideslang taxonomy
------------------
Files:   contract/lib/taxonomy/data_categories.json          (canonical)
         contract/lib/taxonomy/data_uses.json                (canonical)
         contract/lib/taxonomy/data_subjects.json            (canonical)
         plugins/ai-inventory/references/taxonomy/data_categories.json   (verbatim copy)
Source:  https://github.com/ethyca/fideslang
         src/fideslang/default_taxonomy/{data_categories,data_uses,data_subjects}.py
Author:  © Ethyca, Inc.
License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
         https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

This is a MODIFIED redistribution: the upstream Python definitions were reformatted to JSON and
reduced to the `fides_key`, `name` and `description` fields. No other change was made to the
meaning of any entry.

The taxonomy is the bundled vocabulary a piece's validator checks Fideslang keys against, so that
an AI inventory and a Fides privacy data map describe data in the same language. An installed
plugin cannot read a file from outside its own directory, so each piece carries a verbatim copy of
the files its validator loads; scripts/check_vendored_lib.py fails the build if a copy drifts from
the canonical snapshot. Every copy is covered by the same CC BY 4.0 attribution.

Snapshot provenance, and how to refresh it, are documented in
contract/lib/taxonomy/SOURCE.md.

This repository's own code is MIT-licensed. The taxonomy data directory remains CC BY 4.0.
